<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">San Salvador</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1525">1525</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">San <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a> is the capital of El Salvador, founded by the Spanish in 1525 and re-established in 1528 after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pipil">Pipil</a> resistance. A provincial capital within the Captaincy General of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a>, it became in 1834 the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federal-republic-of-central-america">Federal Republic of Central America</a>, whose liberal leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-morazan">Francisco Morazán</a> made it his base until the federation collapsed. It has often been damaged by earthquakes.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/san-salvador.jpg" alt="San Salvador" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Frankjh · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Monumento_al_Salvador_del_Mundo_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
